{"title":"1995 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 1995 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8859dbfb7a9ec734e16f2a88fb5cf1104eb6a39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> be four distinct points on a line, in that order. The circles with diameters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />. The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d13fd509f3062449aaea6e10e1040b1d585063f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> intersects the circle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f874b39870586f0504f50a667f2bafedddf47904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the circle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c68cf05136649b06905dc34a1704d04f394ea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM,DN,XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" /> are concurrent.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e32cfd3a6f5f31f73d0b272a5f7b1638fd16551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2ad1ca4077a0191129259e27550780a3f1fdeb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a^3(b+c)} + \\frac{1}{b^3(c+a)} + \\frac{1}{c^3(a+b)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}.\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d8a348130d140aad5a9c23958578539f753241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> for which there exist <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/5732ee2640c9dc15536ac3513c8bf57c6f02d3ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,\\ldots,A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> in the plane, no three collinear, and real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8cd68021db402d69867e12b162f5b9a69612da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1,\\ldots,r_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"11\" /> such that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/3/4e3045d2f53c7da48801f7843deed6f04f9f6311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i&lt;j&lt;k\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe17cdbb37c534e275c871ba105627dac79283bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle A_iA_jA_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/6/0c608cfe0597d3a478478c6ad0ed22706598b195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i+r_j+r_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/92841bdfe843828d61f7b38ff17b1361a965901d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0, x_1, x_2,.....x_{1994}, x_{1995}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"185\" height=\"11\" /> satisfy the relations \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae2ebb9eafe7224df2b3abca676089e790fcea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0=x_{1995}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/0184cd25ab1b10e36c30defc0f6f03bf96fe31ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i-1}+\\frac{2}{x_{i-1}}=2{x_i}+\\frac{1}{x_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"181\" height=\"39\" /> \n</p><p>for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065ec358741348393366594be9e8a4cb73d9415d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,2,3,....1995$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" /> \n</p><p>Find the maximum value that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> can have.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> be a convex hexagon with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/9576e51c7703b7fb9d7b9e3878732659e4253bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=BC=CD$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cc597e3833d6fed634a4c7dbc6cfc8a19ffdc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=EF=FA$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31b45d09ed5715efbb0eb8f0e6b2a3c67f313e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCD=\\angle EFA=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"174\" height=\"33\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are points in the interior of the hexagon such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36ac93da855ff2a907d13560fd976aa29456da2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AGB=\\angle DHE=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"186\" height=\"37\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a6e698761cadc52b9aa4d787ba0cfd88254d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG+GB+GH+DH+HE\\ge CF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"294\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be an odd prime number. How many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-element subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/17309dbf64d98abe13c87dd70feb9f1ab2c0e1d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1,2,\\ldots,2p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> are there, the sum of whose elements is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO\" title=\"1995 IMO\">1995 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO\" title=\"1995 IMO\">1995 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO\" title=\"1994 IMO\">1994 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_IMO\" title=\"1996 IMO\">1996 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043900\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [s